sentences.l:
Kongzi said of the Ji: “Eight rows dancing in his courtyard —
if this he can bring himself to,
what can he not bring himself to?”

The Master said: “Ci!
You grudge the sheep;
I grudge the rite.”

The Master said: “The ‘Guanju’ —
joyful, and not to excess;
mournful, and not to injury.”

The Master heard of it and said:
“A thing accomplished — one does not discuss;
a thing under way — one does not remonstrate;
what is already gone — one does not blame.”

The Master said: “Dwelling above, not generous;
performing the rites, not reverent;
attending mourning, not grieving —
by what should I observe him?”
